  "edge_schema": "voltmarkt_edge_pat",
  "prompt": "Do deeper discounts lift sales more? For each discount_pct, take the promotions with that discount that started in 2025 (start_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025), work out each one's units on promotion and baseline units, and add them up per discount. A sales line is on a promotion when it carries that promotion's ID in order_lines.promo_id, whatever its date; where two promotions overlap on a product, a line carries only the deeper one, so it counts once. The baseline ends the day before the promotion's start_date and has as many days as the promotion ran, start_date and end_date both counted; it holds every sales line of the promotion's products in those days, whatever promotion the line carries. Days are sales.order_date, the UTC day of the order. A period with no sale counts 0. Then give uplift_pct, the summed promotion units minus the summed baseline units, as a percentage of the summed baseline units, rounded to 1 decimal with ROUND (12.5 for 12.5%), or missing when the summed baseline units are 0. Return five columns, in this order: discount_pct, promotions, promo_units, baseline_units and uplift_pct. Return one row for each discount_pct among those promotions. Any row order is fine.",
  "output_contract": {
    "columns": [
      {
        "name": "discount_pct",
        "type_class": "numeric"
      },
      {
        "name": "promotions",
        "type_class": "numeric"
